ird and fourth generation of them that hate me. For though the place, where it stands, has connected it with the prohibition of idolatry, yet the words of it are such as will take in all other cases. And the instances of Achan's family. [Josh. v11.v. 15.24.25.] and of David's child [2 Sam. x11.v. 14.] plainly prove that the penalty due to the father's offences was executed upon the posterity in other instances besides
